# Flutter Expert

When implementing or modifying Flutter/Dart code in this project:

## Architecture

- [ ] Follow existing layout: `lib/app/` (router, scope), `lib/state/` (stores), `lib/pages/`, `lib/components/`
- [ ] App-wide state in Signals stores (`signal`, `computed`, `listSignal`); expose via `AppScope`
- [ ] Navigation with `go_router`; routes in `lib/app/routes.dart`
- [ ] User strings via `.tr` and `lib/i18n/` — no hardcoded UI copy

## Widgets

- [ ] `const` constructors on static widgets; keys on list items
- [ ] Do not build widget subtrees inside `build()` — extract to methods or widgets
- [ ] Prefer `SignalBuilder` / `Watch` for reactive UI over `setState` for app state
- [ ] Reuse project components (`OpaqueGroupedSection`, `GlassScaffold`, dialogs in `components/`)

## State (Signals)

- [ ] Read with `.value`; write by assigning new values — never mutate in place
- [ ] Side effects in stores, not scattered in widgets
- [ ] Async store methods set loading/error signals; guard `BuildContext` after awaits

## Performance

- [ ] No heavy work on UI thread — use `compute()` for large CPU tasks
- [ ] Profile jank with DevTools before micro-optimizing
- [ ] List views: stable keys, avoid rebuilding entire trees on small signal changes

## Testing

- [ ] Pure logic in testable helpers (see `lib/state/gemma_model_helpers.dart`)
- [ ] Widget tests with `flutter_test`; offline checks via `dart run tool/verify_*.dart` when native deps block `flutter test`

## Must Not

- [ ] `setState` for cross-screen or persisted state
- [ ] Skip `mounted` checks after async gaps with `BuildContext`
- [ ] Import platform APIs directly in widgets — keep in stores or platform layers
